.TH DOHTEST 1
.SH NAME
dohtest \- test the DNS-over-HTTPS wire format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dohtest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Dohtest
checks
.IR doh (2)'s
DNS wire-format encoding and decoding offline \(em no network. The
encode vector is a real Google DoH query captured on the wire
(example.com A, id 0), so
.IR doh (2)'s
.B encode
must reproduce it byte for byte. The decode vectors are hand-built
responses in RFC 1035 wire format including the message-compression
pointers real answers use \(em two A records, and an NXDOMAIN (rcode
3) so the error path is covered.
.PP
There is no live-resolution leg: every current public DoH resolver
serves an ECDSA certificate that
.IR tls12 (2)
cannot yet verify, so a live resolve fails at the TLS handshake. The
wire format \(em the part where bugs actually hide \(em is fully
exercised here; the live path lights up unchanged once ECDSA support
lands. See
.IR doh (2)'s
BUGS.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/dohtest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR doh (2),
.IR dns (1)
.SH BUGS
The negative control \(em corrupting the name-skip in the decoder,
which must break the vectors \(em is run by editing the source, not
automated. Coverage is the wire format only; the transport and
certificate paths are covered by
.IR httpstest (1)
and
.IR tls12test (1).
